FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: buffer_append_n
Signature: int buffer_append_n(buffer_t *self, const char *str, size_t len)
Description: /**
 * @brief Appends a substring to a buffer, resizing if necessary.
 *
 * Copies up to len bytes from str to the end of the buffer's data,
 * resizing the buffer if there is not enough space. The buffer is
 * always null-terminated after the operation.
 *
 * @param self Pointer to the buffer to append to. Must not be NULL and must be initialized.
 * @param str Pointer to the string to append. Must not be NULL. The function copies at most len bytes.
 * @param len Number of bytes to append from str. May be zero.
 *
 * @return Returns 0 on success, or -1 if the buffer could not be resized.
 *
 * @note Error: Returns -1 if memory allocation fails during resizing.
 * @see buffer_resize
 */
Dependencies: buffer_resize

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called buffer_append_n
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <string.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <ctype.h>
#include <sys/types.h>
#include "buffer.h"

// Forward declarations for dependency functions
int
buffer_resize(buffer_t *self, size_t n);

// Target function implementation
int
buffer_append_n(buffer_t *self, const char *str, size_t len) {
  size_t prev = strlen(self->data);
  size_t needed = len + prev;

  // enough space
  if (self->len > needed) {
    strncat(self->data, str, len);
    return 0;
  }

  // resize
  int ret = buffer_resize(self, needed);
  if (-1 == ret) return -1;
  strncat(self->data, str, len);

  return 0;
}

```

